      'LINE-\u20601, about 6000 pairs when complete, is about 17\u00A0per\u00A0cent of the genome in some half a million copies',
      'Alu, about 300 pairs, has over a million copies and about 10\u00A0per\u00A0cent, and cannot move by itself but borrows the machinery LINE-\u20601 makes',
      'insertions that harm the host are removed by natural selection; harmless ones are not, so copies accumulate wherever they are tolerated',
